# Product parity ≠ source copy

NEW app path: `C:\Users\Absm Construction\Desktop\Elix-Star-Live-New`

## Do

- Reproduce the same UI, layout, features, and behaviour as the working product
- Use OLD only as a visual / behaviour / server-contract **reference**
- Write new clean modules (`src/features/*`, `src/services/*`, …)
- Call the **same** production API and WebSocket contracts
- Keep working with existing production data

## Do not

- Copy OLD source (components, hooks, stores, services, giant files, hacks)
- Move OLD files into NEW or recreate OLD architecture
- Rebuild dead / abandoned OLD modules
- Edit or “fix” the OLD application code
- Invent new backend contracts
- Treat “thinner than OLD file” as failure — failure is **missing product experience**

## Measure

PASS = same user-visible experience + correct server result.  
Never aim for source-code parity with OLD.
